-- HYBRID — Exercise library SEED (deduplicated catalog).
-- Run in the Supabase SQL Editor AFTER reference/sql-exercise.sql (which creates
-- the "Exercise" table). Idempotent: re-running skips rows already present (by
-- slug). Populates 209 published custom exercises from
-- reference/exercise-catalog.md so they appear in the web Builder + "Add exercise".
--
-- Field notes:
--  • pattern  — the closest core movement pattern (drives fatigue). Isolation
--    lifts map to the nearest (curls→pull, extensions→push, crunches→core).
--  • muscles  — the coarse engine enum (quads/glutes/posterior/back/chest/
--    shoulders/triceps). NEVER leave this empty: the engines resolve a lift to
--    its muscle groups, so a row with no muscles contributes ZERO load to
--    fatigue, ACWR, injury risk, volume-by-muscle, landmarks and muscle records
--    — the tissue reads as untrained no matter how hard it was worked. Groups
--    the enum lacks map to their coarse home, exactly as core's ENGINE_GROUP
--    already does: biceps + forearms + traps -> back, calves + abs + obliques
--    -> posterior. A coarse attribution beats none. Pinned by
--    packages/core/src/engines/catalog-coverage.test.ts, which fails the build
--    if any row here is empty or unresolvable.
--  • category — the muscle-group heading (library grouping only).
--  • aliases  — folds a built-in / second spelling onto the primary name.

on conflict ("slug") do nothing;
